 subject="yesod-static context changes"
 date="2026-10-09T02:39:04Z"
 content="""
From the `yesod-static` issue (linked above):

> I think the problem is that crypton-1.1.4 now uses ram instead of memory, which is fundamentally incompatible with the current version of yesod-static.

it seems like all of those `yesod-static` / `ram` / `crypton` changes are related, but that the problems people encountered were build issues rather than a runtime issue.  (And the [unmerged yesod-static PR #1916](https://github.com/yesodweb/yesod/pull/1916/files), seems to selectively use `ram` or `memory` depending on the `crypton` version; notably it is unmerged for 4+ months.)

But it does at least seem notable that Homebrew have changed how they're addressing those build conflicts.

Ewen
"""]]
